meta {
  name: Get a blog post
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/blogs/{{id}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:3000
  id: aee8b5b2-db2c-46ef-870c-9fac8f0c45ae
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  # Get a Blog Post
  
  Retrieves a single blog post by its UUID.
  
  ## Endpoint
  `GET /api/v1/blogs/:id`
  
  ## Authorization
  None — this is a public endpoint.
  
  ## Path Parameters
  
  | Param | Type   | Required | Constraints | Description                    |
  | :---- | :----- | :------- | :---------- | :----------------------------- |
  | id    | string | Yes      | Valid UUID   | The unique ID of the blog post. |
  
  ## Success Response
  - **Status Code**: `200 OK`
  - **Body**:
    ```json
    {
      "success": true,
      "message": "Blog found successfully",
      "data": {
        "id": "uuid",
        "title": "Blog Title",
        "description": "Blog description",
        "documentUrl": "https://res.cloudinary.com/...",
        "publicId": "Cedarrise Initiative/BLOG/...",
        "date": "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"
      }
    }
    ```
  
  ## Error Responses
  - **400 Bad Request**: Validation failed (e.g., `id` is not a valid UUID).
  
  ## Notes
  - The result is cached under `cedarrise:blogs:single:{id}` with a 1-hour TTL.
}
